    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a fair point about practical skills, but I'm more worried about the foundational depth. I've seen too many candidates from vocational programs struggle when things move beyond the basics and require a high level of theoretical abstraction. \n\nI'm looking at her raw technical assessment data right now—it's extremely high, basically perfect. But honestly, I'm wondering if a test can really capture whether she has the mental discipline and the \"academic weight\" that someone from a place like MIT would naturally bring. Does her background make you think she might hit a ceiling once she moves past routine execution?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
